    "title": "Waterloo man sentenced to 18 months after cutting ankle monitor, fleeing Cedar Rapids facility - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By KCRG Staff ,\n5 hours ago CEDAR RAPIDS, Iowa (KCRG) - A Waterloo man who cut his ankle monitor and escaped from a residential re-entry facility was sentenced to a year and a half in prison today. In January, Nicholas Campbell-Scott fled from the Gerald R. Hinzman Center in Cedar Rapids and was found almost a week later in Coralville. Read full article\n1",
